  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is a noun?",
      "a": "A noun is a naming word for a person, place, thing or idea, like farmer, Cairo, kite or joy.",
      "asks": [
        "What does noun mean?",
        "Naming words"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a proper noun?",
      "a": "A proper noun is the special name of one person, place or thing, like Priya, Lagos or Monday. It always starts with a capital letter.",
      "asks": [
        "Do proper nouns need capital letters?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Is love a noun?",
      "a": "Yes. Love, courage and joy are abstract nouns: names for feelings and ideas you cannot touch. Love can also be a verb, as in I love mangoes.",
      "asks": [
        "What is an abstract noun?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How can I test if a word is a noun?",
      "a": "Try putting a, an or the in front of it: a kite, the beach, the joy. If it makes sense, it is probably a noun.",
